{"name":"Pink Ribbon","hex":"#f8dae1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"ribbon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long, narrow strip of material used for decoration of clothing or the hair or gift wrapping.","An awareness ribbon."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To decorate with ribbon.","To stripe or streak."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ribbon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pink ribbon","blocks":[{"text":"The pink ribbon is an international symbol of breast cancer awareness. Pink ribbons, and the color pink in general, identify the wearer or promoter with the breast cancer brand and express moral support for people with breast cancer. Pink ribbons are most commonly seen during National Breast Cancer Awareness Month."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink_ribbon","wikidata":"Q1139632"},{"title":"Pink Ribbon (snooker)","blocks":[{"text":"The Pink Ribbon is a pro–am snooker tournament that was initially held at The Capital Venue in Gloucester, England. Established in 2010, the tournament raised funds for breast cancer charities and had the players all wear pink shirts to show their support. Stuart Bingham was the final champion in the initial run."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink_Ribbon_(snooker)","wikidata":"Q15708151"},{"title":"Ribbon","blocks":[{"text":"A ribbon is a thin band of material, typically cloth but also plastic or sometimes metal, used primarily as decorative binding and tying. Cloth ribbons are made of natural materials such as silk, cotton, and jute and of synthetic materials, such as polyester, nylon, and polypropylene. Ribbon is used for useful, ornamental, and symbolic purposes. Cultures around the world use ribbon in their hair, around the body, and as ornament on non-human animals, buildings, and packaging. Some popular fabrics used to make ribbons are satin, organza, sheer, silk, velvet, and grosgrain."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Scrummy_ribbons_by_Lainey_Powell.jpg/330px-Scrummy_ribbons_by_Lainey_Powell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ribbon","wikidata":"Q6918773"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Breast_Cancer_Pink_Ribbon.JPG/500px-Breast_Cancer_Pink_Ribbon.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Breast_Cancer_Pink_Ribbon.JPG/1280px-Breast_Cancer_Pink_Ribbon.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Breast_Cancer_Pink_Ribbon.JPG/500px-Breast_Cancer_Pink_Ribbon.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"100 women who survived breast cancer carry a pink ribbon and create the fight breast cancer logo.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABreast_Cancer_Pink_Ribbon.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Maine_license_plate_breast_cancer_awareness_ribbon.jpg/500px-Maine_license_plate_breast_cancer_awareness_ribbon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Maine_license_plate_breast_cancer_awareness_ribbon.jpg/1280px-Maine_license_plate_breast_cancer_awareness_ribbon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Maine_license_plate_breast_cancer_awareness_ribbon.jpg/500px-Maine_license_plate_breast_cancer_awareness_ribbon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pink ribbon on a Maine license plate, with the slogan \"Early detection saves lives\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaine_license_plate_breast_cancer_awareness_ribbon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Breast_Cancer_Awareness_Month_09.jpg/500px-Breast_Cancer_Awareness_Month_09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Breast_Cancer_Awareness_Month_09.jpg/1280px-Breast_Cancer_Awareness_Month_09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Breast_Cancer_Awareness_Month_09.jpg/500px-Breast_Cancer_Awareness_Month_09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Pink ribbon Philippines Philippine Cancer Society, Inc.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABreast_Cancer_Awareness_Month_09.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Glaube.jpg/500px-Glaube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Glaube.jpg/1280px-Glaube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"